{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For their vine is from the vine of Sodom.</b> He says that the idolaters are destroyers of counsel — they do not succeed, do not understand, and do not devise anything but evil all day long, for from an evil root they came, and they produce only evil and bitter fruit; whoever eats of it shall die. The meaning is that Israel confess, repent, and perform <i>teshuvah</i> in the time of their distress, saying, \"And why has all this befallen us?\" (Judges 6:13). But the idolater, a destroyer of counsel, has no counsel and no understanding; he only follows after his idol and denies the name of the honored One forever, for thus he inherited from his fathers. Behold, he is from a root that yields <i>rosh</i> (gall) and <i>la'anah</i> (wormwood), and there is no benefit in them ever. But Israel, whose root is good — even if it be cut down, it will yet renew itself and produce good fruit."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:58:19.754445087Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}